<!-- Preferences > Colors in the Charis look (research/266 4. prefs-w-view). The Charis page of the tab "colors"
     (floater_preferences.xml: only its filename= points here). Charis's page (from: official
     Second_Life_Release#d567465e-26.5 panel_preferences_colors.xml, left as it is; its functions are all here:
     tools/ui-parity-diff.py). The class is the floater's panel_preference: its saveSettings() / cancel() keep and
     give back the colour of every color_swatch (found under any box: it walks all the children) and the sliders'
     controls; the floater finds the swatch "background" by its name (LLColorSwatchCtrl). The 13 swatches are the
     official widget, each in a glass box (52 x 32, the swatch 44 x 24 at 4 / 4); their colors are the official
     defaults (Pref.getUIColor sets the user's).
     Every row is at a fixed place from the top of the scroll panel (follows left|top): resizing the window only
     changes how much of the page is shown.
     Size (1080 base; plus/prefscharis/prefs_tab_template.xml): 574 x 515; a scroll_container (574) with a panel
     557 wide. Rows at left 14, 529 wide; the swatches on three columns at 14 / 191 / 368 (177 apart), their names
     60 to the right of them, 115 wide (ja at most 8 characters). From the top:
       10 + my effects 24 + 4 + its swatch 32 + 10 + chat font colors 24 + 4 + three rows of swatches 32 + 6 + 32
       + 6 + 32 + 10 + mentions 24 + 4 + swatches 32 + 10 + name tag 24 + 4 + the swatch and the opacity 32
       + 10 + floater opacity 24 + 4 + active 31 + inactive 31 + 14 = 470 (no scroll at the default size; it
       scrolls in a shorter window). The sliders' labels: the opacity 100, active / inactive 200 (ja
       "非アクティブなフローター：" 13 characters, 169). -->
